{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":260352,"duration_api_ms":262645,"num_turns":1,"result":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils reimplements GNU coreutils/moreutils in Go, verified via differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries. The project is an experiment in specification-driven code generation using the mage-claude-orchestrator pipeline.\n\n**Architecture**: Specifications in `docs/specs/` drive code generation into `cmd/<utility>/` packages, with shared infrastructure in `pkg/testutils/` (differential testing), `pkg/sys/` (syscall abstractions), and `pkg/format/` (output formatting). Each utility has `main.go` + `<name>_test.go` with differential tests against GNU `g`-prefixed reference binaries.\n\n**Current state**: 33 releases defined (00.0 through 15.0). Many utilities are implemented. The `requirement_states` field shows which SRD requirements are still \"ready\" (not yet started). The earliest incomplete release with ready requirements is **12.0** (shred, install).\n\n## Priority Analysis\n\n**Release 12.0** is the earliest incomplete release with ready requirements:\n- `srd099-shred`: R3.1, R3.2, R3.3 (3 requirements ready -- R1/R2 groups presumably complete)\n- `srd101-install`: R1.1-R1.4, R2.1-R2.4, R3.1-R3.3 (11 requirements ready -- no code exists yet)\n- `srd100-chroot`: No requirements in ready state (not actionable)\n\nNo dependencies block 12.0 beyond rel00.0 which is already partially implemented.\n\n## Weight Budget Check\n\nAssuming default weight=1 for all requirements (weights not provided in context):\n\n- Task 0: install R1.1(1) + R1.2(1) + R1.3(1) + R1.4(1) = 4 -- OK\n- Task 1: install R2.1(1) + R2.2(1) + R2.3(1) + R2.4(1) = 4 -- OK\n- Task 2: install R3.1(1) + R3.2(1) + R3.3(1) = 3 -- OK\n- Task 3: shred R3.1(1) + R3.2(1) + R3.3(1) = 3 -- OK\n\nCanonical ordering: cmd/install (i) before cmd/shred (s) alphabetically; implementation tasks sequenced by requirement group.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"cmd/install srd101-install R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R1.4 (implementation)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd101-install.yaml (requirements R1.1 through R1.4)\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (shared_protocols section for SIGPIPE and differential testing patterns)\n      - pkg/sys/sys.go (FileInfo, Stat, Lstat for file metadata)\n      - CLAUDE.md (build instructions and SIGPIPE handler requirement)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/install/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"install utility -- initial implementation covering srd101-install R1.1 through R1.4\"\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement srd101-install R1.1 as specified in the SRD. Read the SRD to determine the exact requirement.\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement srd101-install R1.2 as specified in the SRD. Read the SRD to determine the exact requirement.\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement srd101-install R1.3 as specified in the SRD. Read the SRD to determine the exact requirement.\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement srd101-install R1.4 as specified in the SRD. Read the SRD to determine the exact requirement.\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main() per the shared SIGPIPE protocol in ARCHITECTURE.yaml\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use go build -o bin/install ./cmd/install/ to verify compilation. The bin/ directory is git-ignored.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Use standard library os, io, and filepath packages for file operations. Import pkg/sys only if the SRD requires extended file metadata (Stat, Lstat, FileInfo).\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"This is the first of three implementation tasks for cmd/install. Implement only R1.1-R1.4. Later tasks will add R2.x and R3.x requirements.\"\n\n    acceptance_crite